# Code owners for main. "Require review from Code Owners" is on for main, so a
# PR that changes a file listed here cannot merge without approval from one of
# its owners (not the author).
#
# Only .github/ is listed. Workflows there can post commit statuses with the
# same GitHub Actions identity that branch protection trusts, so a PR that adds
# or edits a workflow could fake a required check such as "Lead approval".
# Requiring the Platform & Integration lead or the Team Lead to approve every
# change under .github/ closes that gap.
#
# Area leads are not listed. review-routing.yml already requests them, and the
# "Lead approval" check already requires their approval (see "How review
# routing works" in docs/ROLES.md). Listing them here as well would make every
# area lead a required reviewer of every file in their area, and a lead could
# not merge their own work in that area.
#
# Keep in sync with the Platform & Integration lead and the Team Lead in
# .github/area-leads.json.

/.github/   @MatejPechoucek @danielharrington06
